Subject: DownloadQueue: report a download once without a TTY

Without cursor movement the queue prints only finished downloads. The pass that redraws pending lines prints one
that finished after the partition before it, and the next pass prints it again from finished_downloads. MRI's GVL
makes the window small; under rugaroo the download threads run in parallel and several lines print twice.
---
diff --git a/Library/Homebrew/download_queue.rb b/Library/Homebrew/download_queue.rb
--- a/Library/Homebrew/download_queue.rb
+++ b/Library/Homebrew/download_queue.rb
@@ -261,6 +261,9 @@
               previous_pending_line_count = 0
               remaining_downloads.each_with_index do |(downloadable, future), i|
                 break if previous_pending_line_count >= max_lines
+                # Without cursor movement only finished downloads print, and one that finished since the
+                # partition above is printed by the next pass: printing it here too would print it twice.
+                next if !tty_with_cursor_move_support? && finished_states.include?(future.state)
 
                 last = i == max_lines - 1 || i == remaining_downloads.count - 1
                 previous_pending_line_count += output_message.call(downloadable, future, last)
